OL,2,V55555555CNORIEGA 'TO QUIT
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CBEFORE ELECTIONS'
OL,5, Panama's military strongman Gen Manuel
OL,6, Noriega has promised to resign before
OL,7, general elections are held in May next
OL,8, year,says acting president Manuel Palma
OL,10, But the United States, which has been
OL,11, pushing Gen Noriega to resign, rejected
OL,12, the proposal as totally unacceptable.
OL,14, "We believe the offer is little more
OL,15, than a ploy...an effort by Gen Noriega
OL,16, to maintain control of Panama's defence
OL,17, forces," the State Department said.
OL,19, Opposition leaders in Panama vowed to
OL,20, continue a general strike that closed
OL,21, 90% of businesses yesterday.
OL,23,F]DFrom 22-03-88 / teletextarchive.com
